From: mscharged-port
Subject: Keep DWC_GetDateTime's server time offset in an OSTime
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility; no game behavior change.

DWC_GetDateTime keeps the server time offset in an OSTime, the type
DWCi_Auth_GetServerTimeOffsetInSeconds writes: on 64-bit Linux s64 is
long and OSTime long long, and GCC 14 and later reject the pointer.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_nastime.c b/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_nastime.c
index a91694b..f52eeb9 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_nastime.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_nastime.c
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@ DWCIngamesnCheckResult DWC_GetIngamesnCheckResult(void)

 BOOL DWC_GetDateTime(DWCDate* date, DWCTime* time)
 {
-    s64 diff;
+    OSTime diff;
     s64 localsec = DWCi_Np_GetTimeInSeconds();
     BOOL result = DWCi_Auth_GetServerTimeOffsetInSeconds(&diff);
     struct tm* tm;
